  "term": "compensatory eye movements",
  "definition": "Compensatory eye movements are reflex eye movements produced by signals from the balance organs of the inner ear that travel through brainstem pathways to the eye-movement nerve centers. They help keep the image on the retina stable when the head rotates.",
